  "body": "Consider https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#crossorigingetownpropertyhelper-(-o,-p-) applied to `crossOriginWindow.location`. In particular,\r\n\r\n> If e.[[NeedsGet]] is true, then set crossOriginGet to an anonymous built-in function, created in the current Realm Record, that performs the same steps as the getter of the IDL attribute P on object O.\r\n\r\nThis says that the getter function returned must run the same steps as the getter of location on Window, which are:\r\n\r\n> The Window object's location attribute's getter must return this Window object's Location object.\r\n\r\nThat is, it's asking us to go get the cross-origin Location object, which might be in another process, and return it.\r\n\r\nI think instead what we need to do here is to create an origin-appropriate wrapper for Location and associate it with `crossOriginWindow` + `currentlyExecutingWindow` (~ current Realm). (Or return the already-existing one?) But I cannot see any indication of this in the spec.\r\n\r\nThis seems like it applies for location, top, opener, and parent. Maybe even the indexed properties? Presumably not for window/self/frames although there might be subtle wording problems there.\r\n\r\n@annevk @bzbarsky @bholley; this was discovered by @zetafunction trying to implement in Chrome",
